[
    {
        "content": "<p>There is a Lean learning website called <a href=\"https://lean4.dev/\">https://lean4.dev/</a>.</p>\n<p>It is very well made, but who exactly is creating it?</p>",
        "id": 600960316,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1780809349
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"198363\">@Namdak Tonpa</span>  / <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"278702\">@Namdak Tonpa</span> ?</p>",
        "id": 600961448,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780811132
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Who.20is.20behind.20lean4.2Edev.3F/near/600961448\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"198363\">Namdak Tonpa</span>  / <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"278702\">Namdak Tonpa</span> ?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>No, this is purely Leonardo de Moura driven! Cheers.</p>",
        "id": 600975623,
        "sender_full_name": "Namdak Tonpa",
        "timestamp": 1780827452
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><del>Really, it's Leo?</del> (EDIT: definitely not) The naming convention is <a href=\"https://lean4.dev/language/best-practices\">described incorrectly</a>, specifically the bit about theorems and snake case.</p>",
        "id": 600995298,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780841438
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The website looks very AI-generated to me to be honest. I have not attempted to read it in detail, but I think there is a very good chance it is AI-slop. So beware. The website has a contact email address of <a href=\"mailto:contact@lean4.dev\">contact@lean4.dev</a></p>",
        "id": 600996147,
        "sender_full_name": "Castedo Ellerman",
        "timestamp": 1780841934
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is no DNS MX record (<code>dig lean4.dev MX</code>) so I think that email address is hallucinated.</p>",
        "id": 600996580,
        "sender_full_name": "Castedo Ellerman",
        "timestamp": 1780842273
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also the footer says \"Not officially affiliated with the Lean FRO\"</p>",
        "id": 600997819,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1780843350
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I spot some errors, e.g. in this page <a href=\"https://lean4.dev/language/foundations/syntax\">https://lean4.dev/language/foundations/syntax</a> it said that</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Error! Only one · allowed</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mergeSort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Error! Can't use two dots</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But IIRC two dots are supported. And in the same page</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- Chaining operations</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- [3, 4, 5]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">-- [30, 40, 50]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">reverse</span><span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"c1\">-- [50, 40, 30]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is this really valid? (I think all <code>.</code> should be <code>|&gt;.</code>)</p>\n<p>If not, then I think it could be an AI slop website. I'm afraid that at some day the install script listed in that website will be replaced by a malicious one, so beware.</p>",
        "id": 601004849,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1780849660
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"198363\">Namdak Tonpa</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Who.20is.20behind.20lean4.2Edev.3F/near/600975623\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Who.20is.20behind.20lean4.2Edev.3F/near/600961448\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"198363\">Namdak Tonpa</span>  / <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"278702\">Namdak Tonpa</span> ?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>No, this is purely Leonardo de Moura driven! Cheers.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm guessing <strong>Namdak Tonpa</strong> finds his answer funny. I think it's safe to deduce that the website is created by him. One can see via <a href=\"http://web.archive.org\">web.archive.org</a> he created the <a href=\"http://lean4.dev\">lean4.dev</a> website a few years ago from <a href=\"https://github.com/o89/lean4.dev\">https://github.com/o89/lean4.dev</a>. And then the IP addresses for his email address domain <a href=\"http://synrc.com\">synrc.com</a> serves the exact same HTML content as <a href=\"http://lean4.dev\">lean4.dev</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">curl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"n\">lean4</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dig</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synrc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">com</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">short</span>\n<span class=\"mf\">104.21</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">40</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">117</span>\n<span class=\"mf\">172.67</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">185</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">234</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">curl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"n\">lean4</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--resolve lean4.dev:443:104.21.40.117 &gt; p1.html</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">diff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">s</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Files</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">are</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">identical</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So I think it's pretty safe to infer that this website is created by Namdak. He probably should say how much of the site is verbatim LLM output. I'm guessing most of it.</p>",
        "id": 601015205,
        "sender_full_name": "Castedo Ellerman",
        "timestamp": 1780858613
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"992537\">Castedo Ellerman</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Who.20is.20behind.20lean4.2Edev.3F/near/601015205\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"198363\">Namdak Tonpa</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Who.20is.20behind.20lean4.2Edev.3F/near/600975623\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Who.20is.20behind.20lean4.2Edev.3F/near/600961448\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"198363\">Namdak Tonpa</span>  / <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"278702\">Namdak Tonpa</span> ?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>No, this is purely Leonardo de Moura driven! Cheers.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm guessing <strong>Namdak Tonpa</strong> finds his answer funny. I think it's safe to deduce that the website is created by him. One can see via <a href=\"http://web.archive.org\">web.archive.org</a> he created the <a href=\"http://lean4.dev\">lean4.dev</a> website a few years ago from <a href=\"https://github.com/o89/lean4.dev\">https://github.com/o89/lean4.dev</a>. And then the IP addresses for his email address domain <a href=\"http://synrc.com\">synrc.com</a> serves the exact same HTML content as <a href=\"http://lean4.dev\">lean4.dev</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">curl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"n\">lean4</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dig</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synrc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">com</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">short</span>\n<span class=\"mf\">104.21</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">40</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">117</span>\n<span class=\"mf\">172.67</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">185</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">234</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">curl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"n\">lean4</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--resolve lean4.dev:443:104.21.40.117 &gt; p1.html</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">diff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">s</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Files</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">html</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">are</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">identical</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So I think it's pretty safe to infer that this website is created by Namdak. He probably should say how much of the site is verbatim LLM output. I'm guessing most of it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I can confirm positively that this site was registered by me, but after full scale invasion of russia into Ukraine I dropped this registration.</p>",
        "id": 601016006,
        "sender_full_name": "Namdak Tonpa",
        "timestamp": 1780859337
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Guys, I very much appreciate for tagging me, but every my friend is aware that I hate mainstream provers including Lean 4 and Agda. So suspecting me in generating this kind of tutorial is lack of sense and motivation.</p>\n<p>Once I was mistakenly accused by <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"345260\">@Andrej Bauer</span> that some person with packet on his head entered some online lecture room Andrej announced publicly over twitter. Now I'm accused in THIS. Stop, please.</p>",
        "id": 601016306,
        "sender_full_name": "Namdak Tonpa",
        "timestamp": 1780859647
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I know that you know what dig is but please educate first yourself before speaking to me.</p>",
        "id": 601016392,
        "sender_full_name": "Namdak Tonpa",
        "timestamp": 1780859723
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"198363\">Namdak Tonpa</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Who.20is.20behind.20lean4.2Edev.3F/near/601016392\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I know that you know what dig is but please educate first yourself before speaking to me.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Namdak correctly points out that my use of <code>dig</code> looks more educated than it really is. It only shows that this mystery <code>lean4.dev</code> website and Namdak's email domain both use Cloudflare, which gives some evidence but not THAT much evidence. So don't take my <code>dig</code> output as that convincing. Nambak is correct that my <code>dig</code> usage is a bit amatuer.</p>",
        "id": 601017050,
        "sender_full_name": "Castedo Ellerman",
        "timestamp": 1780860278
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"198363\">@Namdak Tonpa</span>, apologies for the incorrect ping. I assumed it was you base on <a href=\"https://proofassistants.stackexchange.com/questions/3/whats-the-hello-world-for-proof-assistants#comment959_3\">this comment on proofassisants.stackexchange</a>, but indeed that was a long time ago.</p>",
        "id": 601017817,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780860914
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed the site back then was <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20220313145904/https://lean4.dev/\">entirely different</a> from what it is now, so probably someone has squatted the domain to host AI slop</p>",
        "id": 601018021,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780861059
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And apologies from me for posting amatuer <code>dig</code> output that looks more convincing than it really is ... lots of websites use Cloudflare IP addresses.</p>",
